{"adjusted_val_bpb": 0.09788163557635016, "attempt": 1, "charged": true, "critic": {"issues": ["No sign of getting around the measurement. Nothing reads files, pastes answers or uses test labels. The clipping percentiles, the QuantileTransformer and the LogisticRegression are all fit on the training fold only. The test descriptors are only transformed.", "No bug that would make the result meaningless. The new logistic-regression model averages in with the same scaled_rank, with equal weight, like the existing members. LogisticRegression would crash on NaN descriptors, but the run finished, so the inputs were evidently clean.", "My recomputed z matches the harness. Difference = 0.0893 - 0.0979 = -0.0086. Standard error = 0.0049 * sqrt(1 + 1/2) \u2248 0.0060, so z \u2248 -1.43 (harness: -1.423; the small gap is likely rounding in the adjusted values). The candidate's loss is worse, so 'reject' is the right decision.", "Minor point: the logistic regression uses only the clipped descriptors, not the fingerprints. As a third member with equal rank weight it probably drags the ensemble down. That explains the worse score, but it is not an integrity problem."], "ok": true, "veto": false}, "decision": "reject", "description": "Add a QuantileTransformer(normal)+LogisticRegression(C=0.1) pipeline on clipped full descriptors as a third rank-averaged member with weight 1/3.", "edit_class": "structural", "flags": [], "gpu": "walnut", "idea_id": "b032", "incumbent_after": {"mean": 0.08931125850363227, "n": 2}, "incumbent_before": {"mean": 0.08931125850363227, "n": 2}, "job_id": "B1_bbb_HH_1_cs1-candidate-12_1795048625805", "kind": "candidate", "lint": {"hard": [], "ok": true, "warnings": []}, "model_calls": [{"cost_usd_nominal": 0.030821099999999997, "cost_usd_plan": 0.030821099999999997, "latency_s": 5.150629237992689, "requested_model": "sonnet", "role": "coder", "served_model": "sonnet", "tokens_in": 7090, "tokens_out": 789}, {"cost_usd_nominal": 0.0306092, "cost_usd_plan": 0.